  "body": "  The ideal is closed in , and the canonical map is an isomorphism. Give each the subspace topology inherited from , and give the max norm. Then the sequence of topological abelian groups is strict exact. Here the maps are    Lean (ext_pair_injective)  Lean (ideal_row_surjective)  Lean (ideal_pullback_controlled)  Lean (isClosed_IA)  Lean (ext_pair_injective)  Lean (ideal_row_surjective)  Lean (ideal_pullback_controlled)  Lean (isClosed_IA)   For , let be as in the proof of , and let be the corresponding constant for . Take , and choose and such that  In the difference belongs to . Choose such that The norm-preserving coefficientwise section induces a norm-preserving section on second exterior powers; use it to obtain mapping to . Replacing by does not change , and the images of and in now agree. Exactness of , applied coefficientwise, gives mapping to this pair. Then maps to .  These bounds, continuity of , and the norm-preserving coefficientwise section give a constant , independent of , for which satisfies The map is injective, so this proves both the algebraic pullback assertion and the boundedness of its inverse.  It remains to see that is closed. The ideals and are closed by . If lies in the closure of , its images lie in and . The pullback isomorphism just proved gives with the same two images as . Injectivity of gives , as required.  Finally, for choose such that Apply the norm-preserving section and then . This gives mapping to , with bounded by a fixed multiple of . Thus is a strict surjection. Its kernel is by the pullback assertion, and the preceding bound for the inverse makes the inclusion on the left strict. This proves .   "
